I think actually the very first two places we stopped we had one boy and his dad come over and make sure we ordered the right things on the menu.
最初去的两家店里，有一位男孩和他的父亲过来，帮他们确认点了合适的菜。

12
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:07,680
They were cute we then went to a bunker place where we met another guy.
她觉得他们很可爱。后来去另一家店时，他们又遇到了一个人；店铺称呼疑似误识别。

13
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:12,799
That then just stopped and asked us what we'd eaten what we wanted to eat gave us loads of recommendations.
那个人停下来，问他们吃过什么、还想吃什么，并给了许多推荐。

14
00:01:12,799 --> 00:01:16,789
Like it's it's just so nice that people want you to have a good time in their country.
他们觉得，人们希望游客在自己的国家玩得开心，这种心意很好。

15
00:01:16,799 --> 00:01:23,750
Yeah and the recommendations that he got led us to the sweet shop I think it was called fresco's yeah it was fresco.
他们说，正是那个人的推荐，让他们找到了一家甜品店；两人回忆店名是 Fresco。

16
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:27,999
And that was probably my favorite place that we went on all of burns road.
其中一位说，那大概是自己在 Burns Road 去过的所有地方中最喜欢的一家。

17
00:01:27,999 --> 00:01:31,999
And then the guy in there was also very very nice andospitable.
店里的人也非常友善好客；字幕中的 andospitable 拼写待核验。

18
00:01:31,999 --> 00:01:40,950
So it's just it's nice because we got those recommendations from people which led to us having different experiences on our trip that we hadn't necessarily planned.
他们说，当地人的推荐，让他们在旅途中有了原本未必计划好的体验。

19
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:48,160
Obviously in a lot of these places if anyone out there that hasn't seen the video we weren't actually able to pay for a lot of the food that we had.
她补充，如果观众没看过之前的视频，他们吃过的不少食物其实都没能付上钱。

20
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:51,520
And we knew we were expecting this on our second trip on pakistan.
这是第二次去巴基斯坦，他们已经预料到可能会遇到这种招待。

21
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:55,349
So the first time we came we were like oh wow people are giving us this free.
他们回忆第一次来时，很惊讶人们竟然免费送给他们东西。

22
00:01:55,359 --> 00:02:04,870
They himself cannot cannot accept them we are saying that you are our guest oh thank you so much.
片段中有人坚持说不能收钱，因为他们是客人；旅行者连声道谢，部分字幕语法不完整。

23
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:11,760
It is so hard to pay for things here that this time we made sure every time we got something for free we then paid that amount of money forwards.
他们说，这里想付钱太难了，所以这次每逢收到免费招待，就把同等金额的善意传递下去。

24
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:17,840
Onto somebody else whether that be just giving the money or buying food cuz we we don't expect anything for free.
他们可能直接给别人钱，也可能买食物送人，因为他们并不期待免费得到什么。

25
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:25,999
And it's just it's just the general kindness of people this happened all through our trip in pakistan but especially in karachi and on burns road.
他们把这看作人们普遍的善意：整趟旅行都有，尤其是在卡拉奇和 Burns Road。

26
00:02:25,999 --> 00:02:34,559
Like people just didn't want us to pay for stuff and then it's always this kind of weird thing where you try to pay and then.
他们说，当地人不愿意让他们付钱，而自己试图付款时，往往会有些尴尬。

27
00:02:34,559 --> 00:02:40,390
You don't want to feel like you're forcing money on people and then you're offending them in doing that.
他们也不想硬把钱塞给别人，担心这样反倒冒犯了对方。

28
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:47,989
But then this is why we then chose that if we got something for free we would pass this on because that kind of we're still giving back to the community.
因此，他们决定收到免费招待就继续传递，这样也算是在回馈当地社区。

29
00:02:47,999 --> 00:02:52,240
Without trying to force money on someone that wanted to give us a gift.
这样就不用强迫本来想送他们礼物的人收钱。

30
00:02:52,240 --> 00:03:00,800
